                <pb facs="0562" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2690: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morales</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-09-19T17:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 19,
                                1923—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 20—1:25
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>77. The President has [information?] to the effect that a revolutionary movement
                    is being organized in different parts of the country by Gregorio Ferrara
                    assisted by the followers of [Carias?]. The movement is scheduled to take place
                    on the 23rd instant. Martinez Funes is also implicated and he is supposed to
                    invade Honduras from Nicaraguan territory. The President requests that
                    representations be made to the Nicaraguan Government for the reconcentration of
                    Funes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
